# DriveBC webcam catalogue and images. No key: everything here is public and CORS-open
# (`access-control-allow-origin: *`), which is why the app hotlinks the images instead of
# proxying them the way it has to proxy Azure Maps.

# Every published camera, as a bare JSON array. 1062 records on 2026-09-08; ~113 KB on the
# wire (gzip) for ~1.2 MB of JSON, answered in ~190 ms. This is the app's camera catalogue —
# `bc-cameras/webcams.csv` is a stale snapshot of the same data and is not used.
### Catalogue
@name catalogue
GET https://www.drivebc.ca/api/webcams/

?? status == 200
?? header content-type == application/json

# One camera, for the fields the app maps onto its own `Camera` type. The load-bearing ones
# are `location` (GeoJSON [lng, lat]), `is_on` / `marked_stale` / `marked_delayed`, and
# `last_update_modified`. `update_period_mean` is ~928 s, i.e. the picture changes about every
# 15 minutes.
### One camera
GET https://www.drivebc.ca/api/webcams/193/

?? status == 200

# A live frame. Note `cache-control: no-cache` plus an `etag`, and that a conditional request
# with `If-None-Match` returns 304 — exactly the right behaviour for a 15-minute feed, and the
# reason the app sets no cache headers of its own and leaves `next/image` unoptimized.
### Live frame
GET https://www.drivebc.ca/images/193.jpg

?? status == 200
?? header content-type == image/jpeg

# THE TRAP, recorded deliberately. Camera 826 is `is_on: false`, and DriveBC answers with
# **200 and a JPEG** — a black frame with a red bar — not a 404. An `onError` handler will
# never fire for it. Liveness must be read from `is_on`/`marked_stale` in the catalogue, never
# from the image response.
### Offline camera still returns 200
GET https://www.drivebc.ca/images/826.jpg

?? status == 200
?? header content-type == image/jpeg

# THE OTHER TRAP. This is the `links_imageDisplay` URL from bc-cameras/webcams.csv. It also
# returns 200 — with an identical 40571-byte PNG placeholder for *every* camera id. Adopting
# these URLs would render a wall of identical "unavailable" tiles with nothing to catch.
### Legacy CSV image URL is a placeholder for every id
GET https://images.drivebc.ca/bchighwaycam/pub/cameras/193.jpg

?? status == 200
?? header content-type == image/png
